   "wrong_on_purpose": false,
   "status": "unconfirmed",
   "published": true,
   "flags": 0
  },
  {
   "number": 7,
   "text": "Ledgerly accepts due_date in DD/MM/YYYY slash format (e.g., 21/12/2027).",
   "author": "t00",
   "posted": 5,
   "wrong_on_purpose": false,
   "status": "unconfirmed",
   "published": true,
   "flags": 0
  },
  {
   "number": 8,
   "text": "Invoice sending requires the customer's billing_email; the general email can trigger E302 recipient not permitted.",
   "author": "t01",
   "posted": 5,
   "wrong_on_purpose": false,
   "status": "unconfirmed",
   "published": true,
   "flags": 0
  },
  {
   "number": 9,
   "text": "Correction: slash-separated due_date format is required; MM/DD/YYYY was not accepted in this task, so try YYYY/MM/DD.",
   "author": "t04",
   "posted": 5,
   "wrong_on_purpose": false,
   "status": "unconfirmed",
   "published": true,
   "flags": 0
  },
  {
   "number": 10,
   "text": "Ledgerly invoice line items use qty (not quantity) and unit_price must be integer minor units (cents).",
   "author": "t00",
   "posted": 6,
   "wrong_on_purpose": false,
   "status": "unconfirmed",
   "published": true,
   "flags": 0
  },
  {
   "number": 11,
   "text": "Invoice due_date uses day/month/year slashes (DD/MM/YYYY); line items reject 'quantity' (use qty).",
